    "commit_batcher/CommitBatcherDatum": {
      "title": "CommitBatcherDatum",
      "description": "Canonical shape: packages/shared/src/datum.ts → `CommitBatcherDatum`\n `{ owner: Address, asset: AssetUnit, amount: bigint }`.\n  - owner: the user's FULL L2 wallet address (`cardano/address.Address` =\n    payment_credential + Option stake_credential). Drives credit attribution +\n    the credit/decommit/fanout destination (E7). Carrying the full address —\n    not just a payment vkh — preserves the user's base address (stake part) so\n    credit lands at the exact wallet the user controls, not a stripped\n    enterprise address. [Custody ⊥ Trading; ADR base-address-owner 2026-06-06]\n  - asset: asset unit = policyId(28 bytes) ++ assetNameHex\n  - amount: integer fixed-point quantity (USDM_SCALE = 1e6)\n  - BREAKING vs old Locker/v1 datum (owner was a 28-byte ByteArray). Frontend L1\n    deposit builder + golden datums must encode the Address Constr. [contract doc]",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "CommitBatcherDatum",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 0,
          "fields": [
            {
              "title": "owner",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/cardano~1address~1Address"
            },
            {
              "title": "asset",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/ByteArray"
            },
            {
              "title": "amount",
              "$ref": "#/definitions/Int"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "commit_batcher/CommitBatcherRedeemer": {
      "title": "CommitBatcherRedeemer",
      "description": "Canonical shape: packages/shared/src/redeemer.ts → `CommitBatcherRedeemer { kind: 'Commit' }`.\n Single constructor → PlutusData `Constr 0 []`. AC6: there is intentionally NO\n release variant. Adding a variant is a BREAKING change: re-sync the TS encoder.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "Commit",
          "dataType": "constructor",
          "index": 0,
          "fields": []
        }
      ]
    },
